I knew the morning of the 26th that  there was something wrong you could feel  it it was just a sea of fire coming over  the hill burning into the city  from the hospital you could see almost  the whole entire thing  my name is Edd's wada I am a staff  physician at Mercy Medical Center I  provide care for kidney patients and ICU  patients my name is Kenneth Luke I am  the disaster infectious diseases and  basestation coordinator the fire took on  the life of its own  we kept hearing that this fire was  continuing to spread this is a city of  around 90,000 people 30,000 people were  evacuated the red area on this map is  the complete burn from the fire with the  winds being so high and so fast it  actually blew embers over to the other  side of the river which was were a  majority of the homes were burned  I finally planted those roses in the  front of the house and after the fire  they were a puddle of melted plastic  that was what was left of our house I  knew there'd be damage but total  destruction  people were surprised that IDI went back  to work the next day you can't sit  around and mope all that's left now is  the president in future that's not a bad  thing human kindness was displayed  throughout this whole entire event many  many staff lost their homes or evacuated  and just came to work because they knew  that the patients still need to be taken  care of they knew that the community  still needed us from an administration  to a staff they're gonna find a way to  help and they did we set up an Employee  Assistance Program we had a lot of  counselors to come in and set up regular  counseling they set up funds to help  reimburse employees to get them back on  their feet they do supplies available  made some support available make some  money available anybody who has  evacuated anybody who lost their home  they helped them out why are we here if  it's not to help each other human  kindness I think is the responsibility  of every person on this planet  [Music